## What I changed

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RequireOwnerFields.java` — the validate step of the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline. After the existing required-field checks, it now:

```java
// Normalize the telephone: strip every non-digit, then require exactly 10 digits.
String telephone = request.getTelephone().replaceAll("\\D", "");
if (telephone.length() != 10) {
    throw new RequiredFieldsException(List.of("telephone"));
}
request.setTelephone(telephone);
```

## Why this spot

- This is the first step in the pipeline (`RequireOwnerFields` → `BuildOwner` → `SaveOwner` → `RespondWithOwnerCreated`), so the normalized value is written back onto the DTO **before** the MapStruct mapper builds the entity — so the 10-digit value is what gets stored and returned as `telephone`.
- The step binds `@RequestBody` **without** `@Valid`, so the raw input (`"(04) 1234-5678"`) is accepted rather than being rejected by the OpenAPI schema's digits-only pattern before normalization can run.
- Throwing the checked `RequiredFieldsException` routes through the existing escalation handler, which responds **400**, satisfying the reject-when-not-10-digits case.

